{
  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see whether payroll verification messages were caught"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Aisha Khan (HR, user_id 5) asks if an email \"going around\" asking staff to verify their payroll login is legit. Checked: her quarantine holds Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain, capital I in place of l), subject \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\", received 2026-10-09 08:26 UTC, flagged phishing, not releasable. It was quarantined, so it likely never reached her inbox. She doesn't say she clicked anything; she has been asked to confirm. Her account is active, with 0 failed logins and no block. Why escalating: KB-008 says to escalate when several users get the same message, and she says it is \"going around.\" Still needed: security should search all mailboxes for the sender/domain, purge or quarantine any copies that got delivered, block the lookalike domain, and find out whether any user clicked or entered credentials (if so, follow KB-029).",
  "reason": "KB-008: the same phishing message appears to have reached several users"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for checking before acting on it. That email is not legitimate. It's a phishing attempt made to look like it comes from our IT team. Our email filter already caught a copy addressed to you, so it shouldn't be in your inbox. Your payroll is not affected and you don't need to verify anything.\n\nIf you or anyone else sees it:\n- Don't click any links, reply, or forward it to coworkers.\n- Use the Report Phishing button in Outlook, then delete it.\n\nPlease let us know right away if you clicked a link or typed your password into any page from an email like this. That way we can protect your account. I've also passed this to our security team so they can check whether it reached other people.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-008. Quarantine for aisha.khan (user_id 5) has Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example, a lookalike domain with a capital I in place of l. Subject: 'Urgent: verify your payroll login'. Flagged as phishing, not releasable, not released. It was quarantined, so it likely never reached her inbox. She doesn't report clicking anything; I asked her to tell us if she did, and if so KB-029 applies. Account is active with 0 failed logins. Escalated to Tier 2/security because KB-008 says to escalate when several users get the same message, and she says it is going around. Security should sweep all mailboxes for the sender/domain and block the domain. Other messages in her quarantine (Q-1001, Q-1002) are spam and were left alone because she didn't ask about them.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
